\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also watch youtube lets plays of games that fit the Trinity idea - such as say Myst or Obduction or even the awesome adventurers of Tex Murphy, heck even Metroid Prime would work in a Trinity sense. Honestly, watching video games be played seems like a perfect way to get some nifty ideas and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Tex Murphy is a name I haven't heard in decades. I remember playing the original Mean Streets and Martian Memorandum on PC when they came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T13:03:18-07:00","id":1377390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1377383#post1377383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. Tex Murphy is a name I haven't heard in decades. I remember playing the original Mean Streets and Martian Memorandum on PC when they came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tex Murphy is one of those fantastic game systems that should not be forgotten in my opinion. hehe<br /> <br /> Also, as a note there was a Tex Murphy game that came out a few years ago called Tex Murphy the Tesla Effect and its brilliant. I totally recommend looking it up. <br /> <br /> As an aside, the post-apocalyptic environments totally fit post-Aberrant War US.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:51:50-07:00","id":1379725,"title":"","content":"I guess it goes without saying that <b>My Hero Academia</b>, which you can watch on HULU as well as the various anime streaming services, has a lot of potential Aberrant ideas to be mined. <br /> <br /> Also <b>The Boys</b> on Amazon Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:35:13-07:00","id":1379880,"title":"","content":"I just watched Steven Spielberg Amazing Stories. Have some interesting ideas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T20:06:09-07:00","id":1382279,"title":"","content":"6 Undeground is like somebody made a movie script out of their action RPG group\u2019s games and handed it to Michael Bay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:48:40-07:00","id":1382504,"title":"","content":"<b>Scorpion </b>is a perfect example of what you could do with talents in Trinity. It's about a team of geniuses who use science to solve problems ranging from dealing with hi-tech espionage to collecting samples from rare species of bats to pulling off hi-risk rescues using experimental technology. Great inspiration for an Aeon Society or Neptune Foundation campaign. Only one of the characters is really suited for combat so it's a great way to get ideas for challenges that either aren't physical or are physical but more related to environment rather than combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:42:44-07:00","id":1382780,"title":"","content":"Just watched <b>Code 8, </b>on Netflix, ok flick for modern day dystopian Psiads or lower tier Aberrants. Bonus Aeon points for the police drones being carried by larger drones, scanning for DNA and used against powered &quot;criminals&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5961-lazygm","name":"LazyGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:41:27-07:00","id":1383204,"title":"","content":"Repeated on TV here last night and on BBC iPlayer, the two-part documentary <a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b09hlz7w\" target=\"_blank\">Expedition Volcano</a> features an international team of scientists and a safety adviser (who was once a Royal Marine sniper and also works on stunts for Marvel movies and hunts tiger traffickers) rappelling down inside a not-entirely-dormant volcano to find better ways to measure its activity. It's the best documentary Neptune Foundation adventure hook I've ever seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:24:23-07:00","id":1385773,"title":"","content":"I was watching Kong: Skull Island. Honestly, it\u2019s not very Core, but it\u2019s a great example of how to play scale in game. Kong is scale 4 (100 times taller than a human) what make most of the shots, even with heavy weapons, no more than annoying, yet when fighting the other Kaiju it\u2019s like normal size creatures.<br /> <br /> it makes me wonder on a Kaiju story...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reacti