08T20:09:07-07:00","id":1386885,"title":"","content":"When it comes down to intra-system spacelane stories, Belt stories, the cold hard vacuum of space stories, I've found that The Expanse is a very nice inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T06:30:28-07:00","id":1387699,"title":"","content":"I come with a two suggestions. Warehouse 13 is great for if you want inspirationi on what Artefacts might do and function like.If you ever wanted inspiration on how to integrate Flux into a Trinty Core game that's a good place to start. The series also acts as an excellent inspiration for a N.O.E.R campaign if you wanted it to as well. My second suggestion, which actually is technically part of the same TV universe as Warehouse 13, is called Alpha's. It's like X-Men but lower powered. There's inspiration for Nova powers but also for Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:40:36-07:00","id":1387718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1387699#post1387699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I come with a two suggestions. Warehouse 13 is great for if you want inspirationi on what Artefacts might do and function like.If you ever wanted inspiration on how to integrate Flux into a Trinty Core game that's a good place to start. The series also acts as an excellent inspiration for a N.O.E.R campaign if you wanted it to as well. My second suggestion, which actually is technically part of the same TV universe as Warehouse 13, is called Alpha's. It's like X-Men but lower powered. There's inspiration for Nova powers but also for Talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warehouse 13 is great! It\u2019s a bit more than just Talents, There are things that can be explained the same way as dinosaur island, what is great for TC Core and Flux.<br /> <br /> Alphas I would say is about Talents, Psiads and natural Superiors. Talents are seen as supernatural by the ones that know it, Psiads are reasonably focused on their powers, or at least they don\u2019t know they can learns other powers, and Superiors are less powerful than the ones in Aexpansion, but still superhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T09:34:26-07:00","id":1391203,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood &amp; Treasure</b> reaches Freeview TV in the UK tonight (6 on Pick... or 8 if you listen to the announcer...) - reviews mostly land on &quot;harmless fun&quot; but with an art theft expert teaming up with a world-class thief to take on a terrorist seeking ancient weapons on the archaeological black market it sounds like a perfect source of adventures for Triton, Les Fant\u00f4mes and the GCI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T14:13:02-07:00","id":1402679,"title":"","content":"I watched Guns Akimbo on Amazon this week. It was fun, and had some ideas that seemed like they might be fun for Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"