till think Riverdale has potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T11:10:28-08:00","id":1429878,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to do a Talent-based Aeon instead of Psi, <i>The Expanse</i> is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T12:24:06-08:00","id":1429885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1429878#post1429878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to do a Talent-based Aeon instead of Psi, <i>The Expanse</i> is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And ICE, the International Consortium of Ecomining, is <i>right there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T17:12:07-08:00","id":1430004,"title":"","content":"IF you want to think about th sheer weirdness trinity era characters can run into, be it former Nova experiments or long-gone alien societies...<br /> <br /> Well, Forbidden Planet has it all. <br /> <br /> Also, you're able to watch Forbidden Planet, so there's actually no downside to this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T09:37:31-08:00","id":1430879,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think of the game Obduction, by Cyan, the makers of Myst and Riven. In the game there is an unknown alien force that can reach through time and space uses something to pick up people, places, things from one place and then puts them in a secured pocket in another place. <br /> <br /> Imagine during the Aberrant War entire towns go missing, with reporters thinking that they were destroyed. But instead of being destroyed they are scooped up by Mysterious Aliens or Quantum Beings or Novas with a Plan and brought elsewhere. An entire campaign saga could be built around such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T15:14:46-08:00","id":1431080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1429338#post1429338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an old film from the 1960s, one of the few really good films George Hamilton was ever in, called The Power. It's both interesting as a horror film with a hidden Nova for the monster ( hidden from those around him, not the audience) and for a character discovering their power and becoming a monster in their turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Power was an amazing, underrated science fiction movie. It works great as an inspiration for Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Something else that can inspire ideas for Aberrant is the old TV series &quot;The Champions&quot; (1968) about a trio of secret agents who develop stealth nova superpowers. It was exciting and fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","name":"Doctor Zero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T15:58:02-08:00","id":1431091,"title":"","content":"If you didn't catch Birds of Prey because you locked down kinda early by US standards (like me), and you have HBO MAX access, you should watch it. Fantastic Talent fodder. You really don't need to have seen any other DC movie as long as you are familiar with who Harley Quinn and the Joker are. There is like half a throway line about Suicide Squad, which was also fun, but had some issues.<br /> <br /> It really made me want to run/play a crime focused TC:Core game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T19:49:20-08:00","id":1431112,"title":"","content":"A weak show, but with interesting takes on classic Sci Fi tropes is The Starlost. I'd strip the show for ideas and have Trinity Era space explorers find the Ark. It's a vast Nova tech artifact with dozens of human communities in it. <br /> <br /> Exploring the ship, making contact with the communities that live there, and either repairing or evacuating the ship would be good solid campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T12:15:02-08:00","id":1431198,"title":"","content":"To go along with The Phantom, The Shadow would fit Adventure pretty well, although he does possess minor powers.<br /> <br /> Fringe - Is pretty much a team of Talents investigating weird science. There's multiple dimensions and a whole bunch of crazy shennaigans<br /> <br /> Stargate SG1/Atlantis - Talents exploring new worlds and can even have some psiads in there with characters like Jonas and Teyla having minor precognitive ability or being able to mind link with aliens.<br /> <br /> Chuck - spy vs spy where eventually a character is able to gain almost any ability the situation requires spontaneously.<br /> <br /> Travelers - Again probably falls under Weird Science or Soft sci-fi but it's about people form the future sending their minds back in time to try and stop things from going to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11841-vlorax","user":"Vlorax","date":". 01-05-2021, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11841-vlorax","name":"Vlorax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T14:45:40-08:00","id":1431216,"title":"","content":"\u201cHaving minor powers\u201d is something Adventure! handles. Specifically, \u201cclosing mens' minds\u201d (the Shadow's signature power) is in Adventure!.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T15:04:03-08:00","id":1431220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431216#post1431216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cHaving minor powers\u201d is something Adventure! handles. Specifically, \u201cclosing mens' minds\u201d (the Shadow's signature power) is in Adventure!.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, I haven't played Adventure so was mostly just including that as a comparison to The Phantom who is pretty much just a guy in a purple suit with an awesome skull cave.<br /> <br /> Adventure! sounds like the game I could possibly get my father to play since The Phantom and The Shadow are his jam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11841-vlorax","user":"Vlorax","date":". 01-05-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11841-vlorax","name":"Vlorax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T19:17:32-08:00","id":1431240,"title":"","content":"Three more things to watch to inspire Adventure stories:<br /> <br /> <b>Sky Captain and The World of Tomorrow</b>-Jude Law plays a heroic aviator and Gwenneth Paltrow plays a reporter who team up to investigate the scheme of a mad scientist to destroy the world.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fabulous World of Jules Verne</b>-A protege scientist investigate the kidnapping of mentor. It was a Czech movie with art house special effects that made old fashioned line illustration of Victorian science fiction novels come to life. Perhaps you could be mesmerized like I was, or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Le mysterieux docteur Cornelius</b>-A French TV miniseries with an over the top evil plastic surgeon who leads the crime organization the Red Hand to prey upon the rich families, and some of those rich families fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","user":"Doctor Zero","date":". 01-06-2021, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","name":"Doctor Zero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T20:08:08-08:00","id":1431246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vlorax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431220#post1431220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice, I haven't played Adventure so was mostly just including that as a comparison to The Phantom who is pretty much just a guy in a purple suit with an awesome skull cave.<br /> <br /> Adventure! sounds like the game I could possibly get my father to play since The Phantom and The Shadow are his jam</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reminder that <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VonAether/status/1218241665091153925\" target=\"_blank\">the Shadow is canon</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T07:57:20-08:00","id":1431467,"title":"","content":"Firefly/Serenity awesome sci-fi series some lower tech in places - crew of mostly talents and a psion.<br /> Mandalorian and other Star Wars series/movies - many talents and a few psiads<br /> Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets - talents and just plain awesome space based movie<br /> Judge Dredd movies - Dredd definitely had a talent and a psiad as well as some cool tech<br /> Continuum- nice set of talents and tech (maybe a dark star nova mega-genius or two) and probably one superior (supersoldier with some cybernetic enhancements)<br /> bit of a different flavor, but Lord of the Rings is full of talents (and maybe some psiads/novas depending on how you want to represent the wizards and some Q-tech or Nova tech (Rings/Swords...))<br /> Mad Max movies (he is probably a talent and good ideas for blight regions)<br /> Die Hard movies (another talent getting increasingly more powerful)<br /> The Expendables movies (another team of talents)<br /> Mission Impossible movies (talents)<br /> The X-Files (talents and strangeness, good stuff!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T09:19:16-08:00","id":1431692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431246#post1431246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Reminder that <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VonAether/status/1218241665091153925\" target=\"_blank\">the Shadow is canon</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally anything that is both pulp and public domain is canon (with some cases needing reimagining only because the Continuum isn\u2019t a world where white man\u2019s burden imperialists are factually correct)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T09:56:46-08:00","id":1431697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431692#post1431692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally anything that is both pulp and public domain is canon (with some cases needing reimagining only because the Continuum isn\u2019t a world where white man\u2019s burden imperialists are factually correct)</div> </div> </div> </div>They may not be factually correct, but they never were in our world, yet people believed it was and were molded by this, so... you don\u2019t need to change the characters at all, just keep in mind that their point of view is different from the modern.<br /> <br /> In other worlds, if they believe they were better than the others for some scientific theory that was proved not valid latter, they still believed in it as \u201cscience\u201d and were molded by this belief.<br /> <br /> The less controversial example is how Adventure! Era have Telluric energy, that latter was \u201cdiscovered\u201d it was in fact 2 different energies (Quantum and Psi), yet technology based in \u201cTelluric energy\u201d had \u201cscientific validation\u201d and molded the creations of the inspired scientists of the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:02:26-08:00","id":1431711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431697#post1431697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They may not be factually correct, but they never were in our world, yet people believed it was and were molded by this, so... you don\u2019t need to change the characters at all, just keep in mind that their point of view is different from the modern.<br /> <br /> In other worlds, if they believe they were better than the others for some scientific theory that was proved not valid latter, they still believed in it as \u201cscience\u201d and were molded by this belief.<br /> <br /> The less controversial example is how Adventure! Era have Telluric energy, that latter was \u201cdiscovered\u201d it was in fact 2 different energies (Quantum and Psi), yet technology based in \u201cTelluric energy\u201d had \u201cscientific validation\u201d and molded the creations of the inspired scientists of the era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m going to assume you misunderstood what I was saying and are not actually arguing the game should present non-white people as inherently inferior because it\u2019s what a small portion of the world (but majority of white people) believed at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:46:57-08:00","id":1431722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431711#post1431711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m going to assume you misunderstood what I was saying and are not actually arguing the game should present non-white people as inherently inferior because it\u2019s what a small portion of the world (but majority of white people) believed at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. What I mean is that you don\u2019t need to change the characters that are racists for \u201cscientific reasons\u201d, because they believing in this is what made them racists, not the theory itself.<br /> <br /> The example I used was wrong because the theory worked in the example, while the racist theory is just bullshit. I rewrote most of the first 2 paragraphs and ignored the example not firing any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T18:52:57-08:00","id":1431778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1431722#post1431722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. What I mean is that you don\u2019t need to change the characters that are racists for \u201cscientific reasons\u201d, because they believing in this is what made them racists, not the theory itself.<br /> <br /> The example I used was wrong because the theory worked in the example, while the racist theory is just bullshit. I rewrote most of the first 2 paragraphs and ignored the example not firing any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t suggesting changing characters from being racist, I was suggesting not presenting a setting that frames them as correct, as a lot of classic pulp does via its presentation of people of color. Hence needs to shift some of the canon when integrating in media references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T08:06:50-08:00","id":1431832,"title":"","content":"I think it is suggested that (many of) these characters are somewhat a product of their society. If you change that, you should change the characters too (as they formed their viewpoints based on their current societal and scientific understanding, not that of today). Some of the villains in particular may just be plainly racist though. It is one of the issues with any old media, it was also a product of their current society, not ours. Many find some of those upsetting, but they do offer valuable insight as to how views have changed over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T09:52:40-08:00","id":1431845,"title":"","content":"The point is, their society is flawed but so is ours, and there is no need to change it at all, that is what give the setting a flavor. There is no way to create a powerful woman that fight against sexism and for women rights if the society was not sexist, that\u2019s is no way to create a Martin Luther King Jr without racism.<br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t want racist heroes ok, make them non racists or even anti-racists (actively fighting racism), change Quartermain to be less superior to their African friends, but if there was no systemic racism in the 1800s, Africa would never be explored by the Europeans (explored both in the discovering aspect and exploring the natural resources and people), and the merits of UAN would be none.<br /> <br /> A society that point racists as correct is the background to build many heroes fighting for the right causes. A racist hero from a book can be the villain of your campaign, showing how bad a National Hero is is the kind of job for a great group of heroes, member of a inclusive and equalitarian Aeon Society. Safari Jackson was openly sexist, yet he was changed by Crackshot capacities, it\u2019s never too late for a redemption ark for an old Hero, even if it\u2019s a pulpit domain character.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want a world with no prejudice, feel free to adjust. I am just pointing the advantages of a racist/sexist setting dot the game (it doesn\u2019t apply to real life, there is no advantages to have a racist/sexist society in real life).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T08:52:39-08:00","id":1433712,"title":"","content":"Sweet Home. Sorta the Aberrant war if there was no nova age and (most of) the novas were immediately aberrant. Could also be good for some sub-aberrant action...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:06:26-08:00","id":1433731,"title":"","content":"Last night I watched A Wrinkle in Time and had many epiphanies related to psionic and aliens.<br /> <br /> It is not a really mature movie, the thematic is juvenile and the explanations are not more solid than &quot;because I want&quot;, but there are many interesting ideas about the aliens (&quot;they talk colors&quot;, is very Chromatics, for example) and the working of teleportation mainly. There is also a general feel of Mind over Mater, that covers several other aspects of the movie.<br /> <br /> In the end, just the VFX worth watching it if you have Disney+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T11:20:55-08:00","id":1434629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1385773#post1385773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was watching Kong: Skull Island. Honestly, it\u2019s not very Core, but it\u2019s a great example of how to play scale in game. Kong is scale 4 (100 times taller than a human) what make most of the shots, even with heavy weapons, no more than annoying, yet when fighting the other Kaiju it\u2019s like normal size creatures.<br /> <br /> it makes me wonder on a Kaiju story...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have often pondered a setting where Kaiju replace Aberrants for the setting wreckers. With Talents and possibly Psiads forming the Kaiju countermeasure squads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T13:17:56-08:00","id":1434638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1375874-trinity-stuff-to-watch-while-at-home?p=1434629#post1434629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have often pondered a setting where Kaiju replace Aberrants for the setting wreckers. With Talents and possibly Psiads forming the Kaiju countermeasure squads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me wants to create an Ultraman campaign; the players are Talents in the Science Patrol. For the Kaiju fight scenes, Ultraman will be player team controlled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","name":"Doctor Zero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T04:02:20-08:00","id":1434675,"title":"","content":"My inspiration for modern Trinity core - #BloodnTreasure is an adventure series in the style of Indiana Jones, Tomb Raider or Relic Hunter - although much more &quot;down to earth&quot;. The main characters are the former FBI agent and an art thief who are looking for the tomb of Cleopatra and Antony from 30 BCE. The whole series is such a low pulp, where puzzles, break-ins, chases and shootings are the order of the day - but nothing totally over the top. Overall, the climate seems like a modern, slower, B-class Indiana Jones - you can watch the genre as you like. Supposedly very informative historically. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt7712598/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt7712598/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt7712598/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.imdb.com/title/tt7712598/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T17:27:05-08:00","id":1434714,"title":"","content":"The Venture Brothers. The setting is loaded with Talents. Magic and superpowers exist, but can be explained away with flux gadgets (talismans), and weird super science. The rare superbeing always has severe limits or weaknesses more in line with sub aberrant mutants or Superiors than Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T18:04:14-08:00","id":1434800,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s probably more Adventure! than modern Trinity, but I\u2019m off to watch this at the cinema this afternoon: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCToNAb7QGU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCToNAb7QGU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCToNAb7QGU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCToNAb7QGU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit: Having watched it, I\u2019d say there are a few unexpected twists in it, but <span style=\"color:#484848\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Chlo\u00eb Grace Moretz certainly could be a Talent.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 02-08-2021, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T02:38:09-08:00","id":1434823,"title":"","content":"&quot;<b>Macguyver&quot; </b>is a TV series about a secret agent who uses his ingenuity, a Swiss Army knife, and duct tape to solve problems, never a gun. Probably a Talent.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>John Doe&quot; </b>is a TV series about a man who has vast knowledge about everything except his identity. Too bad it was very short lived.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;The Middleman&quot; </b>is a comedy action series about the adventures about a secret agent and his apprentice working for an Organization Too Secret To Know fighting science fictional and supernatural threats. Only 12 episodes, and I wish it had another four more years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8102-doctor-zero","name":"Doctor Zero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}